WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.915
Welcome back to Computer Class. Today you will learn how to create a folder on the desktop of your computer.

2
00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:13.548
A folder is like a box. You put related files inside, so you can find them quickly.

3
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:21.675
Step one. Move the mouse to an empty place on the desktop. Then right-click, using the right button of the mouse.

4
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:28.977
Step two. A menu opens. Click New. Another list opens on the side. Click Folder.

5
00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:37.784
Step three. A new folder appears, and the name is ready to change. Type a name for your folder. For example, My Class.

6
00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:44.796
Step four. Press Enter on the keyboard. Your folder is ready. Double-click it to open it.

7
00:00:45.096 --> 00:00:50.521
Tip: choose short names with no special symbols, so they are easy to find.

8
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:56.688
Now it is your turn. Create a folder called Homework, and another called Photos.

9
00:00:56.988 --> 00:01:01.614
To change a name later, right-click the folder and choose Rename. Well done!

